{"paragraphs":[{"text":"%md\n# About This Lab\n**Objective:** Learn how to combine and split DataFrames\n**File locations:**\n**Successful outcome:**\n**Before you begin:**\n**Related lessons:** Working with DataFrames\n\nCopyright © 2010–2021 Cloudera. All rights reserved.\nNot to be reproduced or shared without prior written consent from Cloudera.\n\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:47:33-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","editorHide":true,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912449_-226468614","id":"20171105-200834_1116095891","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:47:33-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:47:33-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"focus":true,"$$hashKey":"object:1805"},{"text":"%md\n## Overview\n\nIn this module we demonstrate how to combine and split DataFrames.\n\n## Combining and Splitting DataFrames\n\n* Spark SQL supports the usual database-style joins:\n    * Cross join\n    * Inner join\n    * Left semi join\n    * Left anti join\n    * Left outer join\n    * Right outer join\n    * Full outer join\n\n* Joins are expensive in the big-data world\n    * Perform joins early in the process\n    * Amortize the cost over many use cases\n\n* Spark SQL supports the following set operations:\n    * Union\n    * Intersection\n    * Subtraction\n\n* Spark SQL provides a method to split a DataFrame into random subsets","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:47:33-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912452_834936171","id":"20210609-222433_1574519092","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:47:33-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:47:33-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1806"},{"text":"%md\n# Setup\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:47:33-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912453_-1423850704","id":"20181114-164229_902436001","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:47:33-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:47:33-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1807"},{"text":"%md\n# Lesson\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:47:33-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912453_-1626269737","id":"20210609-150445_381117564","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:47:34-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:47:34-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1808"},{"text":"%md\n## Joining DataFrames","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:47:34-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912454_-1916199560","id":"20210609-231102_1173405065","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:47:34-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:47:34-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1809"},{"title":"We will use the following DataFrames to demonstrate joins","text":"%spark\n\nval scientists = spark.read.option(\"header\",\"true\").option(\"inferSchema\",\"true\").csv(\"/duocar/raw/data_scientists/\")\nscientists.show()\n\nval offices = spark.read.option(\"header\",\"true\").option(\"inferSchema\",\"true\").csv(\"/duocar/raw/offices/\")\noffices.show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:47:34-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912454_717283323","id":"20210609-231136_1486159156","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:47:34-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:28-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1810"},{"title":"Cross join","text":"%spark\n\n// Use the `crossJoin` DataFrame method to join every row in the left (`scientists`) DataFrame with every row in the right (`offices`) DataFrame:\nscientists.crossJoin(offices).show()\n","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:28-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912455_-658889427","id":"20210609-231416_373015015","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:28-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:30-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1811"},{"title":"Warning","text":"%md\nThis can result in very big DataFrames!","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:30-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912456_414486464","id":"20210609-231614_1055557420","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:30-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:30-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1812"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\nColumns with the same name are not renamed.\nThis is called the *Cartesian product* of the two DataFrames.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:30-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912457_479747849","id":"20210609-231636_1254576650","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:30-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:30-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1813"},{"title":"Inner join","text":"%spark\n\n// Use the `join` DataFrame method with different values of the `how` argument to perform other types of joins\n\n// Use a join expression and the value `inner` to return only those rows for which the join expression is true:\nscientists.join(offices, scientists(\"office_id\") === offices(\"office_id\"), \"inner\").show()\n\n// This gives us a list of data scientists associated with an office and the corresponding office information.\n\n// Since the join key has the same name on both DataFrames, we can simplify the join as follows:\nscientists.join(offices, \"office_id\").show()\n","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:31-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912458_-777321127","id":"20210609-231821_1865619957","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:31-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:35-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1814"},{"title":"Left semi join","text":"%spark\n\n// Use the value `left_semi` to return the rows in the left DataFrame that match rows in the right DataFrame:\nscientists.join(offices, scientists(\"office_id\") === offices(\"office_id\"), \"left_semi\").show\n\n// This gives us a list of data scientists associated with an office.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:35-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912458_2020695499","id":"20210609-232653_529939127","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:35-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:37-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1815"},{"title":"Left anti join","text":"%spark\n\n// Use the value `left_anti` to return the rows in the left DataFrame that do not match rows in the right DataFrame:\n\nscientists.join(offices, scientists(\"office_id\") === offices(\"office_id\"), \"left_anti\").show\n\n// This gives us a list of data scientists not associated with an office.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:37-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912459_-273956234","id":"20210609-232830_1046047309","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:37-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:39-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1816"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\nYou can think of the left semi and left anti joins as special types of filters.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:39-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912460_-1124341230","id":"20210609-232929_1918392793","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:40-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:40-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1817"},{"title":"Left outer join","text":"%spark\n\n// Use the value `left` or `left_outer` to return every row in the left DataFrame with or without matching rows in the right DataFrame:\nscientists.join(offices, scientists(\"office_id\") === offices(\"office_id\"), \"left_outer\").show\n\n// This gives us a list of data scientists with or without an office.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:40-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912477_-805230427","id":"20210609-232928_637649899","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:40-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:42-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1818"},{"title":"Right outer join","text":"%spark\n\n// Use the value `right` or `right_outer` to return every row in the right\n// DataFrame with or without matching rows in the left DataFrame:\n\nscientists.join(offices, scientists(\"office_id\") === offices(\"office_id\"), \"right_outer\").show\n\n// This gives us a list of offices with or without a data scientist.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:42-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912477_1997896547","id":"20210609-233132_835639263","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:42-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:44-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1819"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\nThe Paris office has two data scientists.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:44-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912478_-1071256544","id":"20210609-233310_197367113","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:44-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:44-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1820"},{"title":"Full outer join","text":"%spark\n\n// Use the value `full`, `outer`, or `full_outer` to return the union of the left outer and right outer joins (with duplicates removed):\nscientists.join(offices, scientists(\"office_id\") === offices(\"office_id\"), \"full_outer\").show\n\n// This gives us a list of all data scientists whether or not they have an office and all offices whether or not they have any data scientists.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:44-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912479_1271462218","id":"20210609-233410_1919989150","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:44-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:53-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1821"},{"text":"%md\n### Example: Joining the DuoCar data\n\nLet us join the driver, rider, and review data with the ride data.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:54-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912479_390310265","id":"20210609-233554_1146424900","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:54-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:54-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1822"},{"title":"Read the clean data from HDFS","text":"%spark\n\nval rides = spark.read.parquet(\"/duocar/clean/rides/\")\nval drivers = spark.read.parquet(\"/duocar/clean/drivers/\")\nval riders = spark.read.parquet(\"/duocar/clean/riders/\")\nval reviews = spark.read.parquet(\"/duocar/clean/ride_reviews/\")","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:54-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912480_-1526755460","id":"20210609-233639_1852715423","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:54-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:57-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1823"},{"title":"Since we want all the ride data, we will use a sequence of left outer joins","text":"%spark\n\nval joined = (rides\n  .join(drivers, rides(\"driver_id\") === drivers(\"id\"), \"left_outer\")\n  .join(riders, rides(\"rider_id\") === riders(\"id\"), \"left_outer\")\n  .join(reviews, rides(\"id\") === reviews(\"ride_id\"), \"left_outer\"))\njoined.printSchema()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:57-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912481_485817488","id":"20210609-233827_952416184","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:57-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:58-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1824"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\nWe probably want to rename some columns before joining the data and remove the duplicate ID columns after joining the data to make this DataFrame  more usable.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:58-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912481_854685329","id":"20210609-233930_2039257022","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:58-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:48:58-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1825"},{"title":"For example, see the `joined` data in the DuoCar data repository","text":"%spark\n\nspark.read.parquet(\"/duocar/joined/\").printSchema","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:48:58-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912482_1838584799","id":"20210609-233913_91627979","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:48:59-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:01-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1826"},{"text":"%md\n\n## Applying set operations to DataFrames\n\nSpark SQL provides the following DataFrame methods that implement set operations:\n* `union`\n* `intersect`\n* `except`","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:01-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912483_1735422823","id":"20210609-234159_1381331125","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:01-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:01-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1827"},{"title":" Use the `union` method to get the union of rows in two DataFrames with similar schema","text":"%spark\n\nval driver_names = drivers.select(\"first_name\")\ndriver_names.count()\n\nval rider_names = riders.select(\"first_name\")\nrider_names.count()\n\nval names_union = driver_names.union(rider_names).orderBy(\"first_name\")\nnames_union.count()\nnames_union.show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:01-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912483_1094272934","id":"20210609-234321_1548059875","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:01-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:10-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1828"},{"title":"Note that `union` does not remove duplicates. Use the `distinct` method to remove duplicates","text":"%spark\n\nval names_distinct = names_union.distinct()\nnames_distinct.count()\nnames_distinct.show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:10-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912484_2037162850","id":"20210609-234423_2092462479","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:11-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:18-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1829"},{"title":"Use the `intersect` method to return rows that exist in both DataFrames","text":"%spark\n\nval name_intersect = driver_names.intersect(rider_names).orderBy(\"first_name\")\nname_intersect.count()\nname_intersect.show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:18-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912486_704125556","id":"20210609-234548_1163824754","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:18-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:28-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1830"},{"title":"Use the `except` method to return rows in the left DataFrame that do not exist in the right DataFrame","text":"%spark\n\nval names_subtract = driver_names.except(rider_names).orderBy(\"first_name\")\nnames_subtract.count()\nnames_subtract.show()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:28-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912488_-2558097","id":"20210609-234546_925355223","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:28-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:36-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1831"},{"text":"%md\n ## Splitting a DataFrame","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:36-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912489_-904528393","id":"20210609-234757_657885115","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:37-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:37-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1832"},{"title":"Use the `randomSplit` DataFrame method to split a DataFrame into random subsets","text":"%spark\n\nriders.count()\nval Array(train, validate, test) = riders.randomSplit(weights=Array(0.6, 0.2, 0.2))\n(train.count(), validate.count(), test.count())\n\n// Use the `seed` argument to ensure replicability:\nval Array(train, validate, test) = riders.randomSplit(Array(0.6, 0.2, 0.2), seed=12345)\n(train.count(), validate.count(), test.count())\n\n// If the proportions do not add up to one, then Spark will normalize the values:\nval Array(train, validate, test) = riders.randomSplit(Array(60.0, 20.0, 20.0), seed=12345)\n(train.count(), validate.count(), test.count())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:37-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912490_-1076065089","id":"20210609-234752_1390806088","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:37-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:44-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1833"},{"title":"Note","text":"%md\nThe weights must be doubles.\nThe same seed will result in the same random split.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:44-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912491_-1424463182","id":"20210609-234752_348698865","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:44-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:44-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1834"},{"text":"%md\n# Lab\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:44-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912492_-1388173671","id":"20210609-150527_79851234","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:44-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:44-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1835"},{"title":"1 - Join the `rides` DataFrame with the `reviews` DataFrame.  Keep only those rides that have a review","text":"%spark\n\n// Count the number of reviews before the join:\nreviews.count()\n\n// Perform a right outer join:\nval rides_with_reviews = rides.join(reviews, rides(\"id\") === reviews(\"ride_id\"), \"right_outer\")\n\n// Count the number of reviews after the join:\nrides_with_reviews.count()\n\n// Print the schema:\nrides_with_reviews.printSchema()\n","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:44-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912493_-271624799","id":"20210609-235614_801953798","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:44-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:48-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1836"},{"title":"2 - How many drivers have not provided a ride?","text":"%spark\n\n// Get the driver IDs from `drivers` DataFrame:\nval id_from_drivers = drivers.select(\"id\")\n\n// Get the driver IDs from `rides` DataFrame:\nval id_from_rides = rides.select(\"driver_id\").withColumnRenamed(\"driver_id\", \"id\")\n\n// Find lazy drivers using a left anti join:\nval lazy_drivers1 = id_from_drivers.join(id_from_rides, id_from_drivers(\"id\") === id_from_rides(\"id\"), \"left_anti\")\nlazy_drivers1.count()\nlazy_drivers1.orderBy(\"id\").show(5)\n\n// Find lazy drivers using a subtraction:\nval lazy_drivers2 = id_from_drivers.except(id_from_rides)\nlazy_drivers2.count()\nlazy_drivers2.orderBy(\"id\").show(5)","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:48-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"scala","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":true},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/scala","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912494_1703774368","id":"20210609-235732_713641342","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:48-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:56-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1837"},{"text":"%md\n# Result\n**You have now:** learned how to combine and split DataFrames.\n\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:56-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912495_-2144368290","id":"20181119-142716_792318228","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:56-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:56-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1838"},{"text":"%md\n# Tear Down\n---","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:56-0800","config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/markdown","fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912499_1997527659","id":"20210609-150643_1464999975","dateCreated":"2026-11-17T12:38:32-0800","dateStarted":"2026-11-17T12:49:56-0800","dateFinished":"2026-11-17T12:49:56-0800","status":"FINISHED","errorMessage":"","progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"$$hashKey":"object:1839"},{"title":"Delete the Livy session","text":"%sh\n\nsessionId=$(curl -s localhost:8998/sessions | jq '.sessions[0].id')\ncurl -s localhost:8998/sessions/$sessionId -X DELETE\n","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-11-17T12:49:56-0800","config":{"editorSetting":{"language":"sh","editOnDblClick":false,"completionKey":"TAB","completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"editorMode":"ace/mode/sh","fontSize":9,"title":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"apps":[],"jobName":"paragraph_1794947912499_-210389378